# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
venv/
.venv/

# Environment variables
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Data (raw images, cleaned images, annotations, GT netlists, per-image
# detection caches) — provenance documented in data/README.md.
# Exceptions: frozen split manifests, the data README and the test-split
# ground truth are versioned — they are the benchmark contribution (C1).
# The test GT is here rather than force-added, because it was force-added
# under its old name and the rename silently dropped 192 files back out.
# Its renders/ are regenerable PNGs and stay out.
data/*
!data/splits/
!data/README.md
!data/gt_test_1024/
data/gt_test_1024/renders/

# Experiment outputs (runs, logs, per-run config snapshots, legacy artifacts)
experiments/

# Model weights
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
weights/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local archives and migration backups (large, regenerable / transferred by hand)
*.zip
*.tgz
*.tar.gz
backups/

# Per-image benchmark artifacts (bulky, regenerable). Summaries, per-image
# CSVs and run metadata ARE committed — they are the reported numbers.
results/**/ledgers/
results/**/netlists/
demo/runs/
# Weld review crops: 56 files at ~1 MB, regenerable with
# scripts/adjudicate_welds.py. The adjudication itself is manifest.csv,
# which IS committed.
results/weld_adjudication/*.png

# VLM batch upload payloads: base64-encoded images, ~200 MB across both
# variants at 3 repeats, fully regenerable from the committed prompts + code.
# They are staged in a temp dir and deleted after upload; this is the guard
# against a stray --jsonl-dir or --keep-jsonl putting them in the history.
# Nothing else in the repo uses .jsonl; `git add -f` if that ever changes.
*.jsonl

# Working scratch. Per-arm sweep configs live here transiently; the
# authoritative copy of every config is the snapshot inside each run's
# results/<run>/run_meta.json, so nothing here needs versioning.
scratchpad/

# Blind-review packet images: byte-identical copies of data/raw photographs,
# regenerable with `scripts/make_blind_packet.py` from the seed recorded in
# results/blind_review/manifest.csv (which also carries each file's sha256, so
# a delivered packet stays verifiable). Dataset images are transferred as an
# artifact and are not versioned anywhere else in this repo — the packet must
# not become the exception that quietly puts 11 MB of Digitize-HCD into git.
results/blind_review/packet/images/
# The 1024 frames the annotator's coordinates are expressed in. Same reasoning:
# regenerable from data/cleaned_1024 by the same script, 5.1 MB, not versioned.
results/blind_review/packet/frames_1024/

# Simulation-coverage results (DC sweep / AC / transient, mentor fix 3b).
# Held out of the repo until the author has reviewed them; promote by removing
# this rule and committing results/sim_coverage/.
results/sim_coverage/

# The manuscript. Kept OUTSIDE this repository by the author's instruction --
# it is a submission in progress and must never be committed here. It lives at
# ~/Documents/manuscript/access.tex; scripts that read it take a path argument
# rather than assuming an in-repo location.
paper/access.tex
*.tex.manuscript

# GT-overlay renders for the validation split: 208 MB of derived PNGs that
# scripts/render_gt_overlay.py regenerates in one command from GT + raw scans.
results/gt_overlay_val/
